{"availability":"available","full":"poulpy-fhe/poulpy","name":"poulpy","description":"A backend agnostic modular FHE library over the Torus using bivariate polynomial representation","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":88,"forks":18,"created":"2024-12-04T09:53:09Z","updated":"2026-10-15T21:03:22Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://squid.cedoor.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:42.253Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:42.253Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:42.253Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:12.227Z","stars":87,"forks":18},{"at":"2026-10-11T02:06:49.164Z","stars":88,"forks":18},{"at":"2026-10-15T21:46:42.253Z","stars":88,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["📖 poulpy.dev: quickstart, architecture, layouts, benchmarks, ecosystem and the documentation for CKKS, binary FHE, security and the API.","Poulpy is a fast and modular FHE library that implements Ring-Learning-With-Errors based homomorphic encryption over the Torus. It adopts the bivariate polynomial representation proposed in Revisiting Key Decomposition Techniques for FHE: Simpler, Faster and More Generic to represent Torus polynomials. Compared with the residue number system (RNS), this representation provides simpler and more reusable arithmetic, a common plaintext space for all schemes, and native bridges between schemes. Poulpy also decouples scheme implementations from the polynomial arithmetic backend by being built from…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/poulpy-fhe/poulpy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"91aa426a837563b44dcb1426aeb74381067b64bef68abc4b856b07308ce34409","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:06.010Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:43.289Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"📖 poulpy.dev: quickstart, architecture, layouts, benchmarks, ecosystem and the documentation for CKKS, binary FHE, sec